# Historical file snapshots under backups/ are frozen point-in-time copies, not
# live dependencies or source. Mark them generated/vendored so GitHub's
# dependency graph skips their package-lock.json/package.json files entirely -
# otherwise every backup becomes its own permanent Dependabot alert + PR target
# frozen at whatever vulnerable state existed when that backup was taken
# (found 2026-06-21: 34 phantom alerts + 8 pointless PRs against backup
# lockfiles). Files stay tracked - this only affects dependency-graph scanning.
backups/** linguist-generated=true
backups/** linguist-vendored=true

# THE HANDOFF LOG IS APPEND-ONLY AT THE TOP, WHICH MAKES IT A CONFLICT MACHINE.
#
# Every session writes its entry at line 3. Two branches that touched completely
# unrelated code therefore collide on the same line, every single time, and the
# "conflict" is never a disagreement — both entries are correct and both belong.
# It has cost a manual resolution on branch after branch, most recently on
# job/6112c0af, whose PR GitHub refused as CONFLICTING when all three of its
# checks were green and `handoff.md` was the ONLY file in conflict.
#
# `union` is git's built-in driver for exactly this shape: it keeps both sides'
# lines instead of raising a conflict nobody would ever resolve any other way.
# Nothing is lost, because nothing was ever in dispute.
#
# This is the rule tre-forged-conductor already runs, ported here after it proved
# itself there. It needs no local git config — `union` is built in, so a fresh
# clone is protected the moment it checks this file out.
#
# NOTE it does not apply to AGENT.md, and deliberately. That file is EDITED IN
# PLACE (test-count floors, rules being tightened), so two branches changing the
# same number is a real disagreement, and `union` would silently keep both — a
# file claiming two different test floors is worse than a conflict that stops
# and asks. Union is only ever right for a log that is appended to.
handoff.md merge=union
